    "updated_at": "2026-11-22T08:51:50Z",
    "body": "Claim released. The overlap rule stops this run.\n\nThe unchanged upstream/main commit 1d5de9aeb reproduces the reported Fanuc refusal in three new tests:\n- swarf_opening_establishes_rotaries_before_fanuc_feed\n- contour5d_opening_establishes_rotaries_before_fanuc_feed\n- flow5d_opening_establishes_rotaries_before_fanuc_feed\n\nThe stamp leaves the opening rapid without a pose. A partial change makes that rapid state the upright pose.\nThe stamp test then passes. All three posting tests still fail with the original unknown-A warning.\n\nThe next required change is in post::dump, in crates/post/src/post/mod.rs:516-532.\nThat function drops the initial upright pose. It writes zero rotary angles only after a previous tilt.\nPR #3306 changes the same function. Its body says it is stacked on #3280.\nThe worker instructions forbid a second stack level. This run makes no post change.\n\nThe local branch is issue/3300-initial-rotary-pose.\nThe uncommitted partial patch is in .claude/worktrees/issue-3300.\nIt includes the new app tests and updated motion assertions. No branch was pushed. No PR was opened.\nFailure logs are in the worktree's ignored .claude/tmp directory.\nThe rate guard is unchanged. Mutation checks, the quick gate, and clippy did not run.\n",
    "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
